@@ -0,0 +1,183 @@
+# LOOKUP-CONTRACT — External Lookup Output Contract
+
+> Last updated: 2026-05-24
+
+## Motivation
+
+External lookups — fetching library docs outside the training cutoff, paging
+through a market API, resolving a Kalshi ticker — are noisy and context-heavy.
+z-harness delegates them to dedicated subagents (`external-lookup`,
+`qt-market-lookup`) rather than letting the main orchestrator thread accumulate
+raw HTML or paginated JSON in its context window.
+
+The **lookup contract** is the shared output envelope that every lookup subagent
+emits. Because both agents produce the same structure, the orchestrator can parse
+them without per-agent branching, and new lookup agents can be added without
+changing any consumer code.
+
+---
+
+## Envelope structure
+
+Every lookup response is a single ≤3 KB UTF-8 Markdown string with this shape:
+
+```
+STATUS: <token>
+
+## Answer
+<synthesized prose — no raw HTML, JSON, or YAML dumps>
+
+## Provenance
+- query: <normalized query string>
+- tools_used: <comma-separated: WebFetch, WebSearch, Bash, Read>
+- sources:
+  - <url or path:line>
+- freshness_ts: <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ>
+- confidence: <high | medium | low>
+- commands:
+  - <verbatim Bash command, if any>
+
+## Unresolved
+<gaps, caveats, suggested follow-up — or "none" if fully resolved>
+
+## Raw artifact pointer
+<path to z-harness/lookup-cache/<sha256>.raw>
+```
+
+_(The `## Raw artifact pointer` section is optional; it is only present when the body would exceed 3 KB.)_
+
+### Key constraints
+
+- The **first line** of the response is always `STATUS: <token>` — no leading
+  whitespace, no blank line before it.
+- **Section order is fixed and load-bearing.** The orchestrator parses sections
+  by heading name; out-of-order headings break parsing.
+- **Total size ≤3 KB** — header + all sections + whitespace combined. This keeps
+  the orchestrator's context footprint predictable.
+- **No raw dumps in `## Answer`.** Cite and summarize; if the full artifact is
+  needed, write it to `lookup-cache/` and add a `## Raw artifact pointer`.
+
+---
+
+## STATUS values
+
+| Value | When to use |
+|-------|-------------|
+| `ok` | Retrieval succeeded. Answer is believed reliable. At least one authoritative source was directly fetched and no interpolation was required. |
+| `partial` | Retrieval ran but the result is incomplete or ambiguous. Covers: HTTP 4xx/5xx, rate-limit (429), no search results, pagination truncation, stale cache (>24h). `## Unresolved` explains the gap and may suggest a follow-up. |
+| `refused` | A verb-blocklist pattern matched, or the query was out of scope (e.g. "place a trade"), or a required auth credential was absent. The first line of `## Answer` must be `Refused: <category> — <detail>` where `category` ∈ `{mutation_blocked, out_of_scope, auth_missing}`. |
+
+Exactly one of these three tokens appears; they are mutually exclusive.
+
+---
+
+## Provenance fields
+
+| Field | Required | Description |
+|-------|----------|-------------|
+| `query` | yes | The originating query string, preserved verbatim (no lowercasing); whitespace normalized for cache-key derivation only. |
+| `tools_used` | yes | Comma-separated subset of `{WebFetch, WebSearch, Bash, Read}`. |
+| `sources` | yes | Bulleted sub-list of URL or `path:line` references actually consulted. |
+| `freshness_ts` | yes | UTC ISO 8601 timestamp of retrieval — **not** the source document's own last-modified date. |
+| `confidence` | yes | See Confidence scale below. |
+| `commands` | yes | Verbatim Bash commands issued, or `n/a` if Bash was not used. Commands are **never truncated** here; truncation may appear only inside `## Answer`. |
+
+---
+
+## Confidence scale
+
+| Value | Meaning |
+|-------|---------|
+| `high` | ≥1 authoritative source directly retrieved; no interpolation needed. |
+| `medium` | Source retrieved but corroboration incomplete, or minor interpolation was required. |
+| `low` | Answer came from a stale cache (>24h), or a single source where corroboration was attempted and failed, or significant interpolation was required. |
+
+Use `high` conservatively. When in doubt, prefer `medium`. A stale cache always
+forces `low`, regardless of other signals.
+
+---
+
+## Examples
+
+### Example 1 — web documentation lookup
+
+**Query:** "pydantic v2 model_validator order of execution"
+
+```
+STATUS: ok
+
+## Answer
+In Pydantic v2, `@model_validator(mode='before')` runs before field validation
+(receives raw input dict). `@model_validator(mode='after')` runs after all fields
+are validated (receives the model instance). Both may be stacked; they execute
+in definition order. Class-level validators run before `@field_validator`.
+
+Source: https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/concepts/validators/#model-validators
+
+## Provenance
+- query: pydantic v2 model_validator order of execution
+- tools_used: WebFetch
+- sources:
+  - https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/concepts/validators/#model-validators
+- freshness_ts: 2026-05-24T14:32:10Z
+- confidence: high
+- commands: n/a
+
+## Unresolved
+none
+```
+
+---
+
+### Example 2 — Kalshi ticker lookup
+
+**Query:** "payout schema for KXHIGHCHI-27MAY15-T70"
+
+```
+STATUS: ok
+
+## Answer
+KXHIGHCHI-27MAY15-T70 is a Kalshi binary contract on Chicago daily high
+temperature for 15 May 2027, strike at 70 °F.
+
+- Contract symbol: KXHIGHCHI-27MAY15-T70
+- Market title: Will the Chicago high temperature exceed 70°F on May 15, 2027?
+- Expiration: 2027-05-15T23:59:00Z
+- Payout schema: binary — YES settles at $1.00 if official high ≥ 70 °F,
+  NO settles at $1.00 otherwise
+- Last price: YES $0.42 / NO $0.58  (as of freshness_ts)
+- Open interest: 1,840 contracts
+
+## Provenance
+- query: payout schema for KXHIGHCHI-27MAY15-T70
+- tools_used: Bash
+- sources:
+  - kalshi-cli get-market KXHIGHCHI-27MAY15-T70 (local client)
+- freshness_ts: 2026-05-24T14:35:02Z
+- confidence: high
+- commands:
+  - kalshi-cli get-market KXHIGHCHI-27MAY15-T70
+
+## Unresolved
+none
+```
+
+---
+
+## Authoring a new lookup agent
+
+Any agent that wants to be a compatible lookup provider must:
+
+1. Emit `STATUS: <token>` as its **first line**, no exceptions.
+2. Produce the four sections in the fixed order: `## Answer`, `## Provenance`,
+   `## Unresolved`, and optionally `## Raw artifact pointer`.
+3. Stay within the **3 KB total** budget; overflow goes to `lookup-cache/`.
+4. Record `commands:` verbatim in `## Provenance`.
+5. Never paste raw HTML, JSON, or YAML into `## Answer`.
+6. Implement a verb-blocklist guard before every `Bash` invocation. The baseline
+   patterns are defined in `agents/external-lookup.md`; domain-specific agents
+   extend them.
+
+The canonical machine-readable version of this contract lives at
+`docs/llm/lookup-contract.json`.  The `doc-fetcher` subagent surfaces it
+automatically whenever a query mentions "lookup", "contract", or "external".
